{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 56, :comments ["<b>Over all the face of the land.</b> Who are 'the face of the land'? The rich." "<b>All that was in them.</b> As the Targum renders: דִּי בְהוֹן עִיבוּרָא." "<b>And he broke for Egypt.</b> שָׁבַר is a term both of selling and of acquiring; here it serves as a term of selling; שִׁבְרוּ לָנוּ מְעַט אֹכֶל — a term of acquiring. And do not say it applies only to grain, for in wine and milk too we find it: ״וּלְכוּ שִׁבְרוּ בְּלוֹא כֶסֶף וּבְלוֹא מְחִיר יַיִן וְחָלָב״ (Isaiah 55)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:09.141274102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}